-- title:
--   Hilbert points versus flat closed subschemes of Pⁿ
-- statement:
--   Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $P \in \mathbb{Q}[t]$, and assume $P$ is realisable: there are a field $K$ and an ideal $I \subseteq K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ closed under taking homogeneous components, together with $d_1$, such that $\dim_K\bigl(K[x]_d / (I \cap K[x]_d)\bigr) = P(d)$ for all $d \ge d_1$. Then there is $D_0$ such that for every $m \ge D_0$ the following holds, where a point of $\mathrm{Point}\,A\,n\,h$ over a commutative ring $A$ means an ideal $I \subseteq A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ closed under homogeneous components whose graded pieces $\mathrm{piece}\,I\,d = A[x]_d/(I \cap A[x]_d)$ are finite projective $A$-modules of rank $h(d)$ at every prime of $A$, and $h = \mathrm{hilbertFunctionOf}\,n\,P\,m$ is $d \mapsto \binom{n+d}{n}$ for $d < m$ and $d \mapsto \lfloor P(d)\rfloor$ (truncated to $\mathbb{N}$) for $d \ge m$: there is an assignment $\Phi$ sending each such point $p$ over each $A$ to a scheme $Z_p$ together with a morphism $\iota_p : Z_p \to \mathrm{Proj}$ of the homogeneous coordinate ring of $\mathbb{P}^n_A$, such that (1) $\iota_p$ is a closed immersion and $\iota_p$ followed by `ProjSpace.π A n` is flat and locally of finite presentation; (2) if $p,q$ are points over $A$ and some isomorphism $e : Z_p \cong Z_q$ satisfies $\iota_p = e$ followed by $\iota_q$, then $p = q$; (3) for an $A$-algebra $B$ and points $p$ over $A$, $q$ over $B$ with $q.I = \mathrm{Ideal.map}$ of $p.I$ along $A \to B$, there is $e : Z_q \to Z_p$ making the square formed by $e$, the structure morphisms of $Z_q$ and $Z_p$, and $\mathrm{Spec}(B) \to \mathrm{Spec}(A)$ a pullback, and with $e$ followed by $\iota_p$ equal to $\iota_q$ followed by `ProjSpace.map A B n`; (4) conversely, any closed immersion $\iota : Z \to \mathrm{Proj}$ over $A$ with $\iota$ followed by the projection flat and locally of finite presentation, whose base change to every algebraically closed field $k$ that is an $A$-algebra arises, in the above pullback sense, from some point $q$ over $k$, is isomorphic over $\mathrm{Proj}$ to some $(Z_p, \iota_p)$; (5) for every point $p$ over $A$, every $d \ge m$ and every $F$ homogeneous of degree $d$, one has $F \in p.I$ if and only if for each $i$ the section of the structure sheaf on $D_+(X_i)$ determined by $F/X_i^{d}$ pulls back to $0$ along $\iota_p$; and (6) the ideal of the kernel ideal sheaf data of $\iota_p$ on the affine open $D_+(X_i)$ is generated by the sections $F/X_i^{d}$ for $F \in p.I$ homogeneous of degree $d$.
--
--   This is the comparison, in the form used for Grothendieck's construction of the Hilbert scheme of $\mathbb{P}^n$, between the functor of homogeneous ideals with prescribed graded ranks ('Hilbert points' for the truncated Hilbert function attached to $P$ at a level $m \ge D_0$) and the functor of flat, locally finitely presented closed subschemes of $\mathbb{P}^n_A$; clauses (5) and (6) record the dictionary in both directions, identifying the degree $\ge m$ part of $p.I$ by vanishing on $Z_p$ and the kernel ideal sheaf of $\iota_p$ by the sheaf attached to $p.I$. It feeds the representability statement [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_scheme_represents_flat_lfp_closedSubscheme_hilbertPolynomial_eq_of_closedImmersionBySections`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_scheme_represents_flat_lfp_closedSubscheme_hilbertPolynomial_eq_of_closedImmersionBySections).
